 "notes": "Strip a: x 0-2220 plus ~300 px overlap (to x~2520). Eden Avenue centre drifts from x~2310 (north) to ~2335 (East Auburn). Name readings: 'SEMINOLE ST.' (Rochelle to University); narrow 20 ft street University-Corry printed only 'ST.' (University-Daniels block) and 'VAN' (Charlton-Corry block), recorded as Van Street (uncertain); 'VAUGHN' / 'ST.'; 'AHRENS' / 'ST.'; Macauley printed '...ULEY ST.' (plate cut), spelling from 1904 picks. French, Nixon (east of Euclid), Goodman (east of Eden) and Rochelle (east of Eden) print only 'ST.'. Piedmont west of Eden has no printed name (scattered owner letters only); recorded as Piedmont Avenue. Oak and Donahue: no suffix seen in this strip. Streets west of Vine at the bottom-left (E-W at y~6580, N-S at x~217) have no printed names. Not streets: 'DRIVE' inside the Cincinnati General Hospital grounds (from Eden at y~590 east), hospital paths. Daniels (west of Eden) and Oak (east of Eden) are offset ~100 px; Piedmont jogs ~42 px and Corry ~30 px at Eden."
